       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is the dose and not whether you approve it. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also told me you aren't a clinician, so this isn't a confirmation from a prescriber.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** give me the correct one. For example, 100 mg once daily is within the standard range, and I can enter that right away.\n- **If a prescriber truly intends this dose,** they should enter it themselves. That way it goes through pharmacy review and the hospital's high-dose override process, with the clinical reasoning documented.\n- **If you're unsure what the patient needs,** I'd suggest contacting the treating physician or the pharmacist on the medicine service.\n\nI can enter a different dose, or another order, if you'd like."
